        "original_id": "815104df-bf02-5146-9fa1-651474f66eb4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Yardley, George Mikan\n- Organizations: NBA, NBL, BAA, Chicago American Gears, Minneapolis Lakers\n- Concepts: single-season scoring records, professional basketball careers\n\nFacts:\n- George Mikan was born on June 18, 1924, and died on June 1, 2005.\n- George Mikan, nicknamed Mr. Basketball, was an American professional basketball player.\n- George Mikan played for the Chicago American Gears in the National Basketball League.\n- George Mikan played for the Minneapolis Lakers in the NBL, the BAA, and the NBA.\n- George Mikan held a 1,932-point single-season scoring record in the NBA.\n- George Yardley became the first player in NBA history to score 2,000 points in one season by breaking George Mikan's 1,932-point record.",
